<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="151" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Hide Signal evidence detail when the caller cannot read the witness (D-142)</title>
    <phase>3 Worklist</phase>
    <gate>038 merged (#1891), #1892 merged</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Data-exposure rule on the Signal read path.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive read filter layered on the secure-family witness rule; query-cost limits matter (uac-r2 K1).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <deps>038</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,security,testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Today the evidence rule (145 write-time redaction; 038 read-time witness rule, `SignalSuppressionService.KeepsDetail`) guards only the D-123 secure wall. A witness communication re-filed to an ordinary matter in another business unit, or unfiled (privately owned), still shows its subject and sender to every reader of the Signal (DI-80 #1873; uac-r2 K2 on #1891). The owner decided (D-142): hide the detail from any reader who cannot read the witness.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE BFF engineer.</role>
  <goal>Every Signal read path that returns evidence lines returns a witness's detail (subject, sender, text, source) only when the caller can read that witness row; otherwise the line carries `withheld: true`, exactly as a secure-wall withhold does.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>D-142 (notes/decisions.md); #1873 comments; `notes/task-038-signal-read-route.md`; the walker batching in #1892 (`SecureRootsAboveEachAsync` read-ahead).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalSuppressionService.cs (KeepsDetail :686, WitnessOf, WitnessItemsAsync / WitnessFamiliesAsync :654-680)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReadService.cs (worklist read path; OBO caller reads)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <justification>
    <existing>The secure-wall withhold and the `withheld: true` line shape exist; the caller-identity (OBO) Dataverse read exists in SignalReadService.</existing>
    <extension>Add a caller-readability input to the existing KeepsDetail decision; no new route or registration.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A user sees the subject and sender of a communication they cannot open, contrary to D-142.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-142">Readability is decided by the CALLER's own (OBO) read of the witness rows: one batched query per witness table per request (In lists of at most 200 ids), never one per witness. A witness the caller's read does not return: detail withheld.</constraint>
    <constraint source="fail-closed">A fault in the caller read withholds every detail on the page (the list itself unchanged), as the 038 placement fault does.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">Apply to every route that returns evidence lines (the worklist and any per-Signal route that returns evidence; list them in the notes). The secure-wall rule stays as it is and is evaluated as well (both must keep).</constraint>
    <constraint source="write-time">The 145 write-time redaction cannot know future readers. Do NOT change it unless a rule using existing ownership primitives clearly matches D-142; otherwise record it as a known limit in the notes with a self-contained `ontology-deferred` issue + DI row.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-123">uac-r2 reviews the PR (SendMessage + #1355). Logs carry counts and type names only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">Publish-size delta vs a fresh build of origin/master, no new HIGH CVE; report the query count for 4 and 24 Signals before and after.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read KeepsDetail, the witness collection and the OBO read path.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the batched caller read and pass readability into the keep decision.</step>
    <step order="3">Tests (filtered), seeding proof, query counts, size delta, PR into docs/ontology-platform-design.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A witness the caller can read, outside any secure family: detail shown.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a witness in another BU's ordinary matter the caller cannot read: detail withheld (`withheld: true`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an unfiled, privately owned witness the caller cannot read: withheld.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A secure-family witness the caller can read while the Signal is ordinary: still withheld by the existing rule.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A fault in the caller read withholds every detail on the page and does not change the list.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Query count: one caller read per witness table per request, pinned by a test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">Test scope: the cases above only; seeding proof on the caller-unreadable withhold.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the change requires editing uac-r2's SecureChildShareSynchronizer.cs, STOP and report what is needed.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
</task>
